## Context

The 2026-07 home-directory reorganization moved every project out of `~`.
The nightbeat supervisor (2026-07-11 run) re-pointed `scripts/projects.json`
to the new locations, confirmed by git remote:

- git-erg → `~/CNRS/code/git-erg`
- chemin-de-voix → `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/chemin-de-voix`
- padme → `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/padme`
- climate-finance-het → `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/climate-finance-het`
- aedist-technical-report → `~/CNRS/papiers/actif/AEDIST-technical-report`
- fuzzy-corpus → `~/CNRS/papiers/actif/Fuzzy Corpus`

`cadens` is the one project with no git checkout anywhere on doudou:
`~/data/projets/cadens/` holds only a `raw/` data directory, and no
directory named cadens under `~/CNRS` is a repository. Its registry entry
was removed rather than left pointing at the dead `~/cadens` path.

## Actions

1. Author decides: clone cadens back onto this machine (where?), or retire
   it from the nightbeat perimeter.
2. If restored, re-add its entry to `scripts/projects.json`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] cadens either has a working checkout registered in
      `scripts/projects.json`, or is confirmed retired from the registry
- [ ] `python3 scripts/nightbeat-supervisor-survey.py` runs warning-free
